# Fetched source, cmake trees, and the libraries themselves. Nothing built belongs in
# git: the point of this repo is that the *release assets* are the artifacts, and a
# committed .a is one nobody can tell apart from the one CI made.
build/
dist/
.DS_Store

# The same rule, applied to the Rust half. `prebuilt/` is a cache: ./sync-prebuilt.sh
# fills it from dist/, and failing that crates/libopus-prebuilt-sys/build.rs downloads
# what it needs from the release. What *is* committed is prebuilt.sums — the checksum of
# every release asset, which pins the bytes without storing them.
crates/libopus-prebuilt-sys/prebuilt/
target/
Cargo.lock
